.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt STDNORETURN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm stdnoreturn
.Nd non-returning function specifier
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdnoreturn.h
.Fn noreturn "function declaration"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.In stdnoreturn.h
header defines the
.Fn noreturn
macro, which expands to the
.Va _Noreturn
function specifier.
A function declared with it does not return to its caller and must not be
called in a context that expects it to.
.Pp
The macro is intended for C only.
In C++ the equivalent facility is the
.Va [[noreturn]]
attribute, and the header defines nothing.
.Pp
In ISO C23
.Va _Noreturn
is deprecated in favour of the
.Va [[noreturn]]
attribute, but the
.Fn noreturn
macro and its expansion are unchanged.
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.In stdnoreturn.h
header conforms to
.St -isoC-2011
and ISO/IEC 9899:2024 (C23).
.Sh HISTORY
The
.In stdnoreturn.h
header appeared in
.Ox 8.0 .
